0.1 % (m/v) with 25 mM ammonium bicarbonate, pH 8.5. Trypsin (Promega) was added at a 1:20 enzyme:protein ratio followed by incubation at 37°C overnight. RapiGest was then degraded by addition of 40 \uf06dl of 5 % (v/v) trifluoric acid followed by incubation for 2h at 37°C. Degraded RapiGest was removed by centrifugation and tryptic peptides were dried in a vacuum centrifuge. Cross-linked di-peptides were enriched by peptide size-exclusion chromatography on an SuperdexTM peptide 3.2/300 column using an ÄKTA pure chromatography system (GE Healthcare). For this, the peptides were dissolved in 60 % (v/v) acetonitrile, 0.1 % (v/v) trifluoric acid followed by isocratic separation at a flow rate of 50 \uf06dl/min. Elution of the peptides was monitored at 280 nm. Fractions of 50 \uf06dl were collected. Fractions containing cross-linked di-peptides as well as linear peptides were dried in a vacuum centrifuge and dissolved in 2 % (v/v) acetonitrile/ 0.1 % (v/v) formic acid for LC-MS/MS analysis. For labelling with sulfo-NHS-acetate, a total protein amount of approx. 30 \uf06dg was incubated with 5 and 10 mM sulfo-NHS-acetate for 15 min at 23 °C. The proteins were then precipitated and digested with RapiGest and prepared for LC-MS/MS analysis as described for cross-linked proteins.  For labelling with DEPC, a total protein amount of approx. 30 \uf06dg was incubated with 5 and 10 mM DEPC for 10 min at 37 °C. The proteins were then precipitated as described above. The protein pellet was dissolved in 8 M urea in 25 mM Tris-HCl pH 7.9 followed by incubation for 15 min at room-temperature. The proteins were reduced with 5 mM dithiothreitol for 30 min at 23°C followed by alkylation with 20 mM iodoacetamide for 30 min at 23°C. The solution was then diluted with 100 mM ammonium bicarbonate, pH 8.5 to a final concentration of 2 M urea. Tryptic hydrolysis was performed at 37 °C overnight (enzyme:protein 1:20). Generated peptides were desalted using ZipTips (Merck).\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-